<section class="fragment-instrument" data-artifact="instrument" data-slice="viewer-pitch">
  <table class="in-signals">
    <thead><tr><th>Signal</th><th>Kind</th><th>Side</th><th>Where</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>viewer.connected</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>page</td><td>web/socket.mjs:open</td><td>protocol.version, engine.version, match.id, owner.id, origin, ticks_expected, so a screenshot is attributable to an engine and a match.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>viewer.socket_drops</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>page</td><td>web/socket.mjs:close/error</td><td>match.id, tick, code, wasClean, reason. The contract reserves this key at line 65.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>viewer.tick_skipped</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>page</td><td>web/schedule.mjs:scheduler</td><td>tick, skipped, speed, window_s. One row per second, only when the count is above zero.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>viewer.lag</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>page</td><td>web/playback.mjs:estimator</td><td>requested_speed, sustained_speed, tick, notice_shown. The evidence for AC-5, which no server message supplies.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>viewer.frame_budget</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-gauge">gauge</span></td><td>page</td><td>web/schedule.mjs:rolling window</td><td>frames, fps_median, frame_ms_p95, dropped_frames, refresh_hz, window_s. One row per five seconds.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>viewer.history</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-gauge">gauge</span></td><td>page</td><td>web/history.mjs:keyframe</td><td>ticks_stored, history_bytes (exact), page_bytes (browser gauge, null until resolved), budget_bytes 314572800.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>viewer.rewind</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>page</td><td>web/playback.mjs:scrub commit</td><td>from_tick, to_tick, exact. The exact flag is the AC-6 assertion in signal form.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>viewer.decode_refused</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-log">log</span></td><td>page</td><td>web/decode.mjs:refusal</td><td>reason, tick, bytes, kind. A bad frame is named rather than swallowed as a stutter.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>web.serving</td><td><span class="in-kind in-kind-event">event</span></td><td>engine</td><td>crates/engine-cli/src/web.rs:bind</td><td>dir (relative), files, isolated, port. The isolated flag reports whether the two headers the memory gauge needs are on.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">The page-side signals have no transport</div><div class="callout-body">The observability contract closed U-2 for the engine with a file sink plus the socket feed. Neither reaches a browser: a page cannot write a file, and the socket carries engine-to-page messages, not page-to-engine records. Until a browser path exists, every page-side signal is one JSON Lines row on console.info plus a 256-row ring buffer at window.__touchline.signals, which a browser drive and a Node test can both read. That is enough for verify and not enough for a dashboard. The product owner chose this work knowing the cost (plan Round 3 Q12, options 2 and 3 together); /wf observability owns closing it.</div></aside>

  <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">record.kind: viewer-event is a fifth kind</div><div class="callout-body">The contract's Block A names four record kinds and this is not one of them. Emit it as the additive extra content.hash, teams, and change.queue_id already are, and let /wf observability audit settle whether it is a kind of its own or a variant of match-event. Spell viewer.socket_drops exactly as the contract reserves it, underscore included, so the reservation is honoured rather than shadowed by a near-miss name.</div></aside>

  <style>
    .fragment-instrument .in-signals { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-instrument .in-signals th, .fragment-instrument .in-signals td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); vertical-align: top; }
    .fragment-instrument .in-kind { font-size: 0.8rem; border-radius: 999px; padding: 1px 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.4); white-space: nowrap; }
    .fragment-instrument .callout { margin-top: 12px; }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-instrument');
      var signals = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.in-signals tbody tr').length : 0;
      var dark = 5;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'instrument', artifact: 'instrument', counts: { signals: signals, darkPaths: dark, pii: 0 } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
